1
00:00:08,377 --> 00:00:33,837
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:03,922 --> 00:02:07,922
No animals were hurt during
the filming of this series.

3
00:02:08,925 --> 00:02:12,925
Episode 92

4
00:02:13,430 --> 00:02:15,420
Come on, my lions!

5
00:02:15,763 --> 00:02:19,763
We will reap the rewards of our efforts
in conquest.

6
00:02:19,987 --> 00:02:22,397
Come on, my lions! Work!

7
00:02:33,335 --> 00:02:36,015
Wow, Blacksmith! Wow!

8
00:02:53,894 --> 00:02:58,164
Alps! Protect the catapults!

9
00:02:58,349 --> 00:03:00,629
Hide the swords!

10
00:03:25,975 --> 00:03:29,975
Burn! Burn everything!
Everything!

11
00:03:36,108 --> 00:03:38,418
Sir Blacksmith.

12
00:03:54,976 --> 00:03:57,156
Blacksmith Davut Bey!

13
00:03:58,375 --> 00:04:02,555
Did you make all this preparation for me?

14
00:04:03,643 --> 00:04:05,543
I am honored.

15
00:04:05,813 --> 00:04:09,543
These catapults, these swords...

16
00:04:18,553 --> 00:04:22,553
Look, I've burned them all!

17
00:04:22,865 --> 00:04:24,715
What will you do now?

18
00:05:29,639 --> 00:05:33,079
You've burned them all, Nikola.
You did.

19
00:05:40,569 --> 00:05:44,619
Do you know the Phoenix?

20
00:05:45,781 --> 00:05:47,641
Its name is Turk.

21
00:05:49,856 --> 00:05:57,316
We resurrect if we get burned with
the belief in Islam in our hearts.

22
00:06:15,014 --> 00:06:17,824
Burn it, Nikola.
Burn it.

23
00:06:18,467 --> 00:06:21,387
Your fire in the afterlife will be plenty.

24
00:06:23,011 --> 00:06:25,341
I don't like stories, Blacksmith Bey.

25
00:06:25,690 --> 00:06:29,690
But you Turks love a story very much.

26
00:06:30,393 --> 00:06:33,703
And you talk too much.

27
00:07:01,652 --> 00:07:06,622
Damn it! Inhisar is gone!

28
00:07:07,936 --> 00:07:09,666
Bilecik is gone!

29
00:07:11,257 --> 00:07:15,257
Yarhisar and Inegöl will also be gone,
Lord Basilius.

30
00:07:16,046 --> 00:07:18,526
I don't think so, Commander.

31
00:07:22,421 --> 00:07:24,471
What can stop the Turks?

32
00:07:25,382 --> 00:07:29,692
Their siege will never succeed.

33
00:07:30,092 --> 00:07:33,432
Because they will lose everything they
have.

34
00:07:35,629 --> 00:07:37,939
And they will fail!

35
00:07:42,133 --> 00:07:45,343
They are up to something, my Bey.
They are going to make a move.

36
00:07:47,181 --> 00:07:49,941
You mean, he seemed pretty confident,
right?

37
00:07:54,049 --> 00:07:56,459
How would they know?

38
00:07:58,589 --> 00:08:00,949
-Cerkutay.
-Yes, my Bey?

39
00:08:01,175 --> 00:08:03,045
Beat Aktemur a little.

40
00:08:03,878 --> 00:08:05,768
Then take him to his tent.

41
00:08:07,341 --> 00:08:10,521
As you order, my Bey.

42
00:08:11,389 --> 00:08:12,589
Come on.

43
00:08:26,352 --> 00:08:31,662
Praise be! Our valiants arrived!

44
00:09:14,313 --> 00:09:15,853
Master Davut!

45
00:09:22,117 --> 00:09:23,467
Master Davut!

46
00:09:27,324 --> 00:09:29,754
Master Davut! Are you all right?

47
00:09:29,754 --> 00:09:31,934
I am fine, my Bey. You go after that dog!

48
00:09:32,850 --> 00:09:36,040
-I can't leave you alone, Master Davut!
-I am here brother, come on!

49
00:09:36,170 --> 00:09:40,170
These wounds are nothing to me.
Go after that dog, my Bey!

50
00:09:40,954 --> 00:09:43,124
-Come on brother!
-All right!

51
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:14,232
Come on, valiants, come with me!

52
00:10:16,931 --> 00:10:18,161
Samil!

53
00:10:20,823 --> 00:10:22,263
We are going after my Bey!

54
00:13:14,608 --> 00:13:16,258
Nikola!

55
00:13:33,863 --> 00:13:35,283
Nikola!

56
00:13:36,466 --> 00:13:37,796
My Bey!

57
00:13:41,402 --> 00:13:43,502
Bring him to me after I go.

58
00:13:43,719 --> 00:13:45,579
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order.

59
00:13:53,217 --> 00:13:55,127
My Bey hunted one of the biggest
preys.

60
00:13:56,388 --> 00:13:59,828
If we have Nikola, the fall of Inegol
must be soon.

61
00:14:01,029 --> 00:14:05,459
Lord Nikola! His cruelness was mentioned
everywhere.

62
00:14:07,084 --> 00:14:11,264
Fly in the ointment.

63
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:14,308
The suffering Nikola caused us is not
little at all.

64
00:14:15,643 --> 00:14:17,113
Duty awaits. Come on!

65
00:14:39,776 --> 00:14:43,086
How much time and effort have
we put into these!

66
00:14:43,186 --> 00:14:45,036
All of it got wasted.
All of it!

67
00:14:45,572 --> 00:14:49,332
We can replace what got burned but...

68
00:14:49,332 --> 00:14:52,812
...if I don't see that dog Nikola
burn like this...

69
00:14:52,885 --> 00:14:54,485
...I won't get relief.

70
00:14:56,510 --> 00:14:59,630
I agree, brother. I agree.

71
00:15:24,384 --> 00:15:27,354
Nikola?
Did he run away, Osman Bey?

72
00:15:29,853 --> 00:15:32,113
He is our prisoner.

73
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:35,786
Alps are with him. He is coming
to the tribe with us.

74
00:15:39,568 --> 00:15:41,598
Why are we taking him with us, Osman Bey?

75
00:15:41,903 --> 00:15:43,543
Why didn't you slit his throat?

76
00:15:43,696 --> 00:15:45,126
We should destroy that dog!

77
00:15:45,188 --> 00:15:46,898
I need him alive.

78
00:15:47,774 --> 00:15:52,094
I will let him go when we take Inegöl
Castle.

79
00:15:56,392 --> 00:15:58,342
Are we going to bargain for the conquest?

80
00:16:02,912 --> 00:16:06,912
After all he has done to our brothers it
doesn't suit us to release him.

81
00:16:09,066 --> 00:16:10,396
Osman Bey.

82
00:16:10,961 --> 00:16:13,211
Do we go after a feud, Turgut Bey?

83
00:16:15,002 --> 00:16:17,032
We go after justice.

84
00:16:21,067 --> 00:16:26,597
Could anything be better than taking
Inegol Castle by sparing a dog's life?

85
00:16:27,144 --> 00:16:28,484
Tell me.

86
00:16:29,750 --> 00:16:32,690
You are right. Inegöl first.

87
00:16:32,878 --> 00:16:34,068
Inegöl first.

88
00:16:54,791 --> 00:16:57,301
What if they don't accept the exchange,
my Bey?

89
00:17:00,964 --> 00:17:03,294
Then, we will use Turgut Bey's way.

90
00:17:07,232 --> 00:17:09,712
Are we powerful enough to use that way,
Osman Bey?

91
00:17:12,910 --> 00:17:14,910
Everything is ruined.

92
00:17:19,799 --> 00:17:21,519
We have many martyrs.

93
00:17:24,336 --> 00:17:26,326
They have worked very hard until
this day.

94
00:17:26,906 --> 00:17:31,157
They were forging swords day and night
for the conquest.

95
00:17:39,981 --> 00:17:41,811
May all of them rest in peace.

96
00:17:41,838 --> 00:17:42,938
Amen.

97
00:17:45,686 --> 00:17:46,666
Amen.

98
00:17:47,610 --> 00:17:48,780
But...

99
00:17:50,369 --> 00:17:52,489
...we won't waste their efforts.

100
00:17:54,889 --> 00:17:57,049
We won't stop because we got burned.

101
00:17:59,323 --> 00:18:01,623
We will attack with everything we have,
Brother.

102
00:18:02,995 --> 00:18:06,995
With everything we have!

103
00:18:09,256 --> 00:18:11,906
Nephew, you will go to Inegol.

104
00:18:15,312 --> 00:18:19,752
As if you were a commander who was
taken prisoner, you will tell them...

105
00:18:23,249 --> 00:18:25,709
...that I want the Inegöl Castle...

106
00:18:29,091 --> 00:18:30,611
...in return for Nikola.

107
00:18:36,044 --> 00:18:37,634
As you order, my Bey.

108
00:18:47,386 --> 00:18:49,346
Bury our martyrs.

109
00:18:51,369 --> 00:18:52,759
Where is Master Davut?

110
00:18:52,825 --> 00:18:55,335
He is further.
Alps are checking his wound, my Bey.

111
00:18:56,964 --> 00:18:58,124
Come on.

112
00:19:44,355 --> 00:19:46,005
My brave grandma.

113
00:19:51,017 --> 00:19:54,517
She used to tell us about my grandma
Halime and grandfather Ertugrul Gazı.

114
00:19:56,691 --> 00:19:58,621
Their love was so great.

115
00:19:58,869 --> 00:20:02,869
Is that so? Did they love each other
that much?

116
00:20:03,073 --> 00:20:04,783
So much.

117
00:20:05,884 --> 00:20:09,024
Selcen Mother used to always tell us about
them before our bedtime.

118
00:20:10,004 --> 00:20:13,794
I am very curious. I wish I could
hear it as well.

119
00:20:14,898 --> 00:20:18,608
My grandfather Ertuğrul faced opposition
of everyone for my grandmother Halime.

120
00:20:18,608 --> 00:20:21,418
He saved her from the infidels and brought
her to his tribe.

121
00:20:22,361 --> 00:20:24,491
Didn't he fear anyone?

122
00:20:26,377 --> 00:20:28,137
Would a Kayı valiant ever?

123
00:20:28,521 --> 00:20:32,001
My grandfather Ertuğrul was very brave
even when he was young.

124
00:20:33,043 --> 00:20:36,053
He was not defeated by the enemy,
neither inside nor outside.

125
00:20:38,193 --> 00:20:40,133
My grandmother fell in love with him.

126
00:20:42,038 --> 00:20:46,038
My grandfather Ertuğrul went out for
gazelle hunting, but he went...

127
00:20:46,046 --> 00:20:47,996
...and fell in love with my grandmother.

128
00:20:49,211 --> 00:20:53,681
My grandmother Halime stayed with him
until she died.

129
00:20:56,532 --> 00:20:58,132
What an epic love.

130
00:21:12,383 --> 00:21:16,033
You should have heard their love
from my grandmother Selcen.

131
00:21:19,993 --> 00:21:21,593
She would tell it so differently.

132
00:21:23,575 --> 00:21:25,035
My brave grandmother.

133
00:21:28,843 --> 00:21:30,093
My valiants!

134
00:21:33,264 --> 00:21:36,424
My valiants!
Osman Bey is back in the tribe.

135
00:21:37,119 --> 00:21:41,119
He even prisoned that dog Nikola!

136
00:21:42,994 --> 00:21:45,114
Who could ever stand against my father?

137
00:21:47,632 --> 00:21:49,542
Nikola's payment will be severe.

138
00:21:50,529 --> 00:21:53,719
Come on, then! Let's go to the tribe!
Come on.

139
00:23:37,759 --> 00:23:39,589
Master Davut is wounded!

140
00:23:39,623 --> 00:23:42,323
Take him to the healing tent with alps,
Kumral Abdal.

141
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:50,007
You will die, Nikola! You deserved this!
You will die in pain!

142
00:24:01,808 --> 00:24:04,398
Don't let him live even one more moment!

143
00:24:04,398 --> 00:24:07,458
Inegöl Castle

144
00:24:19,345 --> 00:24:20,855
Stop! Who are you?

145
00:24:22,760 --> 00:24:25,410
There are things I have to tell about
Lord Nikola.

146
00:24:25,538 --> 00:24:27,998
What will you say?
Who sent you?

147
00:24:29,618 --> 00:24:32,478
I am one of the commanders who was
taken prisoner in Bilecik.

148
00:24:33,407 --> 00:24:35,387
Osman took Lord Nikola prisoner as well.

149
00:24:36,900 --> 00:24:38,400
He sent me for the bargain.

150
00:24:38,463 --> 00:24:40,823
I need to speak to a senior commander.

151
00:24:41,758 --> 00:24:44,548
How could this happen?
Come with me.

152
00:24:47,316 --> 00:24:48,756
What happened to Nikola?

153
00:24:50,324 --> 00:24:53,634
Could he ruin the headquarters?

154
00:24:54,582 --> 00:24:56,632
Are you the top commander?

155
00:25:02,919 --> 00:25:04,339
Who is asking?

156
00:25:09,778 --> 00:25:11,878
Here is the greatest commander!

157
00:25:15,102 --> 00:25:19,102
Not only the Inegöl's but also the Rome's
greatest commander!

158
00:25:23,383 --> 00:25:25,563
I don't like compliments, Arius.

159
00:25:26,331 --> 00:25:32,241
The only thing that encourages me is
the painful screams of the people I kill.

160
00:25:37,346 --> 00:25:38,806
Who are you?

161
00:25:39,114 --> 00:25:43,514
I am Alexander, one of the commanders that
Osman took prisoner.

162
00:25:44,311 --> 00:25:45,681
Alexander.

163
00:25:50,406 --> 00:25:54,176
When did Great Rome's commanders start
to get prisoned...

164
00:25:55,201 --> 00:25:56,801
...instead of dying!

165
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:21,170
You are talented, young commander.

166
00:26:22,159 --> 00:26:23,829
I am glad you didn't die.

167
00:26:28,134 --> 00:26:29,584
Tell me.

168
00:26:31,149 --> 00:26:36,749
Nikola destroyed the headquarters.
But Osman caught him.

169
00:26:37,436 --> 00:26:39,546
They have him. He is wounded.

170
00:26:39,903 --> 00:26:43,273
Osman wants to bargain with you.
Thus, he sent me.

171
00:26:45,897 --> 00:26:50,607
Why did Osman send you?

172
00:26:54,096 --> 00:26:55,696
Why did he trust you?

173
00:26:56,587 --> 00:26:58,607
You were free.

174
00:26:59,734 --> 00:27:02,034
You could've run away in peace.

175
00:27:07,333 --> 00:27:10,733
Would a Turk ever trust us, Sir?

176
00:27:11,556 --> 00:27:13,506
Osman didn't trust me.

177
00:27:14,693 --> 00:27:16,273
He compelled me.

178
00:27:18,419 --> 00:27:20,759
He was going to kill my soldiers
if I didn't come.

179
00:27:22,853 --> 00:27:27,483
What a loyal commander is Alexander!

180
00:27:29,487 --> 00:27:31,997
Are you loyal to your soldiers as well,
Romanos?

181
00:27:33,774 --> 00:27:39,954
Commanders are not loyal to their soldiers
soldiers are loyal to commanders.

182
00:27:41,370 --> 00:27:45,010
Because the leaders win the war, not
the soldiers.

183
00:27:51,878 --> 00:27:54,478
What does Osman want in return for
Nikola?

184
00:27:57,896 --> 00:28:01,506
Aya Nikola for the Inegöl Castle.

185
00:28:02,426 --> 00:28:07,296
If you deliver the castle he will free my
soldiers and Nikola.

186
00:28:15,908 --> 00:28:21,078
First Bilecik, now Inegöl...

187
00:28:24,413 --> 00:28:27,683
...you talk no good, Alexander.

188
00:28:30,266 --> 00:28:32,656
I believe I have to cut it!

189
00:28:34,751 --> 00:28:38,041
There's no point in feeling the anger
of defeat, Romanos.

190
00:28:39,921 --> 00:28:42,571
Nikola isn't gone in vain.

191
00:28:42,571 --> 00:28:47,151
Our aim was to destroy the headquarters
and he managed it.

192
00:28:47,752 --> 00:28:50,182
Do you think this will stop Osman?

193
00:28:51,142 --> 00:28:55,142
He won't be satisfied with it. He will
build that headquarters again.

194
00:28:55,216 --> 00:28:58,676
He maybe would if I wasn't going to take
over his mines tomorrow.

195
00:28:59,135 --> 00:29:03,625
But, Osman won't be able to do anything
without his mines.

196
00:29:04,139 --> 00:29:08,439
What about Nikola? Will we leave him
to Osman?

197
00:29:08,518 --> 00:29:09,998
I can't let that happen.

198
00:29:11,495 --> 00:29:13,555
We will think about this offer
for a while.

199
00:29:14,504 --> 00:29:16,474
You can be our guest in the castle.

200
00:29:17,546 --> 00:29:19,286
I am grateful, Sir.

201
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:22,960
I hope you can find a way to save
my soldiers and Aya Nikola.

202
00:29:36,329 --> 00:29:38,359
We won't think about this offer.

203
00:29:39,754 --> 00:29:42,404
Inegöl will never be Osman's!

204
00:29:43,699 --> 00:29:50,069
No soldier is more precious than Rome's
lands!

205
00:29:51,133 --> 00:29:55,813
I won't leave my best student to Osman!

206
00:29:56,743 --> 00:29:59,572
I've already made my plan.
Trust your master.

207
00:29:59,572 --> 00:30:00,433
Trust your master.
I've already made my plan.
Trust your master.

208
00:30:00,433 --> 00:30:01,562
Trust your master.

209
00:30:01,562 --> 00:30:06,292
You aren't my master.
I'm not your student.

210
00:30:09,099 --> 00:30:12,289
I grow up drinking blood!

211
00:30:12,959 --> 00:30:15,819
I walked through fire!

212
00:30:16,202 --> 00:30:20,202
Now, whatever you do,
be quick!

213
00:30:20,492 --> 00:30:25,732
Or, I'll go to Constantinople, build
an army and attack the Turks!

214
00:30:28,413 --> 00:30:35,503
Your anger and army aren't
needed, Romanos.

215
00:30:36,556 --> 00:30:40,726
Because, Barkın will save Nikola.

216
00:30:48,281 --> 00:30:51,451
Take him too!

217
00:30:52,198 --> 00:30:56,198
But he won't die so easily.

218
00:31:12,781 --> 00:31:15,181
My children!

219
00:31:15,689 --> 00:31:20,259
Come!

220
00:31:25,751 --> 00:31:28,721
My lions!

221
00:31:39,916 --> 00:31:42,956
We have martyrs.

222
00:31:43,478 --> 00:31:46,448
But we don't have mourning!

223
00:31:47,905 --> 00:31:53,665
That vile Nikola raided our camp
where we were preparing the conquest.

224
00:31:55,506 --> 00:31:58,855
Our alps have fallen martyrs.

225
00:32:00,435 --> 00:32:05,345
A valiant's bones turn to dust
but he gets remembered.

226
00:32:06,823 --> 00:32:10,823
We'll remember them with
their heroism...

227
00:32:10,823 --> 00:32:15,373
their efforts and their bravery!

228
00:32:18,265 --> 00:32:22,265
We'll remember their part on the
path to the conquest.

229
00:32:24,231 --> 00:32:27,751
They opened the path to the conquest.

230
00:32:30,872 --> 00:32:36,552
We have Nikola. Either they give
the castle and take Nikola...

231
00:32:37,699 --> 00:32:43,279
or we'll behead Nikola and
conquer the castle.

232
00:32:44,682 --> 00:32:49,112
It's their decision.
And it's our jihad!

233
00:32:49,112 --> 00:33:15,255
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

234
00:33:15,777 --> 00:33:20,767
-How is Koses?
-He's in the tent. Waiting for you.

235
00:33:28,958 --> 00:33:34,188
It'll be fine, Davud.
Your wound will heal.

236
00:33:34,582 --> 00:33:38,582
The catapults burned.

237
00:33:40,799 --> 00:33:44,799
They brought the weasel who
inflicted the wound, Master Davud.

238
00:33:45,614 --> 00:33:49,614
My friend Davud!

239
00:33:49,614 --> 00:33:52,614
Are you still alive?

240
00:33:55,297 --> 00:33:59,967
You still breathe because my bey
ordered so, Nikola. Don't test me.

241
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:05,940
Kumral Abdal, Osman Bey wants him
alive for now.

242
00:34:10,554 --> 00:34:15,494
Death and life are from Allah.

243
00:34:16,599 --> 00:34:20,228
My job is causing healing.

244
00:34:22,002 --> 00:34:26,942
He is wounded. But if he can speak,
his hands won't stay idle.

245
00:34:26,942 --> 00:34:29,952
We should chain him.

246
00:34:30,185 --> 00:34:35,005
Don't be afraid if Nikola draws
his weapon but be afraid if he speaks.

247
00:34:35,005 --> 00:34:38,635
This is what this dog deserves.

248
00:34:39,485 --> 00:34:43,485
Since you still can't kill me...

249
00:34:43,485 --> 00:34:48,364
you all need me.

250
00:34:48,969 --> 00:34:52,969
It's the end of your reign, Nikola.
Shut up!

251
00:35:05,803 --> 00:35:08,693
Osman's loyal dogs!

252
00:35:09,653 --> 00:35:13,653
Gencebey! Gag him!

253
00:35:22,479 --> 00:35:25,769
May Allah bless your hands.

254
00:35:39,570 --> 00:35:43,860
Alright. Alright.
As you say.

255
00:35:44,136 --> 00:35:48,636
I'll stay out of this war.
But I want to help you secretly.

256
00:35:48,636 --> 00:35:52,076
Thank you, Koses.
Thank you.

257
00:35:52,076 --> 00:35:56,746
But we won't act careless
like that.

258
00:35:58,353 --> 00:36:02,723
I know, you always supported me.
You risked your life.

259
00:36:02,723 --> 00:36:08,053
But if you get involved with
the conquest of İnegöl...

260
00:36:08,849 --> 00:36:13,529
then, the emperor will have
capitulations on you.

261
00:36:15,871 --> 00:36:20,901
He will. But I'm not afraid of that.

262
00:36:21,693 --> 00:36:26,003
I know, Koses.
Of course, I do.

263
00:36:26,757 --> 00:36:30,757
But stay back for now.
Be ready.

264
00:36:31,520 --> 00:36:36,140
We'll fight a lot. We'll fight
shoulder to shoulder.

265
00:36:37,111 --> 00:36:42,061
But act like an enemy for now.

266
00:36:43,390 --> 00:36:47,710
Alright. What do you want me to do?
Tell me.

267
00:36:48,144 --> 00:36:50,814
Should I build an army?

268
00:36:52,186 --> 00:36:56,186
Yes. But the emperor...

269
00:36:56,335 --> 00:37:00,335
will think that you are building
it against me.

270
00:37:01,802 --> 00:37:06,482
But you'll build an army to
fight alongside me.

271
00:37:08,302 --> 00:37:11,072
Very well.

272
00:37:11,210 --> 00:37:15,590
Let's say it didn't happen as you say.
They didn't give the castle.

273
00:37:15,690 --> 00:37:20,810
Your catapults and weapons
are damaged. What will you do?

274
00:37:20,810 --> 00:37:25,170
Since my grandfather Süleyman Shah and
my father Ertuğrul Ghazi...

275
00:37:25,170 --> 00:37:29,170
we were careful with two things...

276
00:37:29,170 --> 00:37:32,390
weapons and measures.

277
00:37:34,378 --> 00:37:39,748
We don't put all the fruits in the same
basket. The big one is still in the bag.

278
00:37:40,761 --> 00:37:44,761
Good. I see it now.

279
00:37:44,761 --> 00:37:47,271
Tomorrow, İnegöl's walls will
get hit hard.

280
00:37:47,271 --> 00:37:51,271
If they don't give it in peace...

281
00:37:51,480 --> 00:37:54,170
that will happen.

282
00:38:01,974 --> 00:38:04,434
Tell me...

283
00:38:05,633 --> 00:38:08,193
what's happening?

284
00:38:09,659 --> 00:38:13,659
I don't know, Osman Bey.
But for some reason...

285
00:38:14,512 --> 00:38:19,102
I don't feel like returning to
that gloomy castle.

286
00:38:20,810 --> 00:38:25,630
I don't know. Maybe I'm not as
nimble as I used to be.

287
00:38:26,647 --> 00:38:31,407
I don't know. Maybe my
soul is tired.

288
00:38:32,612 --> 00:38:37,882
All these treacheries, my losses...

289
00:38:40,762 --> 00:38:45,012
I saw that light only once again.

290
00:38:46,856 --> 00:38:52,006
When I got wounded,
when Edebali prayed over my head...

291
00:38:53,988 --> 00:38:57,988
I didn't understand what he said...

292
00:38:58,516 --> 00:39:03,036
but it felt like a sparkle in my soul.

293
00:39:03,036 --> 00:39:08,166
I saw that light once again
for a short while.

294
00:39:10,839 --> 00:39:15,979
Koses. That's Allah's grace...

295
00:39:16,718 --> 00:39:19,728
and mercy.

296
00:39:20,019 --> 00:39:24,599
We burn with that fire when
we go to jihad.

297
00:39:25,765 --> 00:39:29,765
If you felt this from the prayer
over your head...

298
00:39:30,279 --> 00:39:34,599
just think about what you'll feel
when you pray to your creator.

299
00:39:40,581 --> 00:39:46,151
You are on the right path. Inshallah,
Allah will put us on the same line...

300
00:39:48,463 --> 00:39:51,973
not only on the battlefield
but also on the salaat.

301
00:39:54,904 --> 00:39:56,724
Thank you.

302
00:39:59,364 --> 00:40:01,824
Thank you.

303
00:40:18,224 --> 00:40:21,044
May I enter, Ayşe Hatun?

304
00:40:35,546 --> 00:40:39,536
-Aktimur!
-Mother!

305
00:40:49,873 --> 00:40:52,693
Aktimur!

306
00:40:53,831 --> 00:40:56,011
Aktimur!

307
00:40:57,726 --> 00:41:01,136
My son! My son!

308
00:41:03,505 --> 00:41:07,505
My Allah, thank you!

309
00:41:07,505 --> 00:41:11,215
You brought me my son!

310
00:41:16,702 --> 00:41:20,702
Many gratitude!

311
00:41:22,588 --> 00:41:26,588
Happiness is soon, mother.
But we need a little bit more patience.

312
00:41:27,693 --> 00:41:32,553
Don't I know it, son? I've been
grinning and bearing it.

313
00:41:32,553 --> 00:41:34,543
I know it.

314
00:41:34,935 --> 00:41:38,935
What can we do?
We'll bear a little longer.

315
00:41:38,935 --> 00:41:43,025
Oh, my son.
You are standing.

316
00:41:43,025 --> 00:41:47,025
Come, let's sit.
Come. You traveled.

317
00:41:47,025 --> 00:41:53,145
I'll prepare you a meal. You must be
thirsty. Let me give you sherbet.

318
00:41:53,620 --> 00:41:58,190
Mother, I'll leave. I must be in
the captive tent.

319
00:41:58,530 --> 00:42:03,180
But you just came. You just came.
Come, sit.

320
00:42:03,180 --> 00:42:06,510
-Let's sit.
-Mother.

321
00:42:07,188 --> 00:42:11,188
Aktimur. Let's sit.

322
00:42:17,808 --> 00:42:21,808
Alright. Alright.

323
00:42:23,358 --> 00:42:26,738
You have my prayers, son.

324
00:42:26,738 --> 00:42:30,738
May Allah guide you.

325
00:42:30,738 --> 00:42:34,738
Be victorious with Osman Bey.

326
00:42:35,445 --> 00:42:39,445
Return to your tribe and mother.

327
00:42:40,065 --> 00:42:42,885
Mother!

328
00:42:48,051 --> 00:42:52,051
Mashallah.
Mashallah.

329
00:42:53,818 --> 00:42:57,818
You grew up!
Mashallah.

330
00:43:03,925 --> 00:43:06,085
Kızılbeyoğlu Tribe

331
00:43:06,180 --> 00:43:10,740
Thank Allah, Osman Bey is saved. And
you didn't make the mistake of taking Söğüt.

332
00:43:11,283 --> 00:43:15,283
Thank Allah. Thank Allah.
But...

333
00:43:15,485 --> 00:43:19,805
you know why I did it.

334
00:43:19,805 --> 00:43:24,335
-I only want the best for our tribe.
-I know it.

335
00:43:24,630 --> 00:43:29,160
I know, but, I couldn't
sleep since we talked.

336
00:43:29,160 --> 00:43:33,160
I was feeling nervous.

337
00:43:33,160 --> 00:43:38,070
Osman Bey and his tribe stood
with us during our difficult times.

338
00:43:41,572 --> 00:43:46,082
Are preparations complete?
You didn't tell anyone anything, right?

339
00:43:46,082 --> 00:43:50,272
As you said, my bey.
No one else knows the road.

340
00:43:50,272 --> 00:43:53,892
I'll be their guide.

341
00:43:53,892 --> 00:43:58,272
When you reach the upland, I'll get
the rest of the people.

342
00:43:58,573 --> 00:44:03,123
Inshallah, my bey. I should be
busy with the preperations.

343
00:44:12,886 --> 00:44:17,686
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come in, Hüsamettin.

344
00:44:25,757 --> 00:44:29,437
The men are ready and waiting
for order, my bey.

345
00:44:31,269 --> 00:44:35,269
You'll be among the ones going
to the upland.

346
00:44:35,269 --> 00:44:40,219
-Don't fight back. I don't want blood.
-As you order, my bey.

347
00:44:41,367 --> 00:44:45,367
-Hüsamettin.
-My bey.

348
00:44:46,909 --> 00:44:50,909
If Selvi gets hurt in
any way.

349
00:44:53,421 --> 00:44:56,691
I'll kill you all.

350
00:45:23,465 --> 00:45:28,335
Both grief and happiness
are for humans.

351
00:45:31,264 --> 00:45:36,164
Everything comes from our creator.

352
00:45:37,289 --> 00:45:41,439
We had losses,
funerals...

353
00:45:42,266 --> 00:45:45,226
We had martyrs...

354
00:45:45,226 --> 00:45:49,226
but thank Allah that...

355
00:45:49,648 --> 00:45:53,828
they all died on the right path.

356
00:45:55,811 --> 00:46:00,941
Selcan Hatun put effort to gain
Allah's aproval...

357
00:46:02,045 --> 00:46:06,045
until her last breath.

358
00:46:07,883 --> 00:46:11,883
May Allah treat her with mercy.

359
00:46:11,883 --> 00:46:15,883
-Amin.
-Amin.

360
00:46:16,084 --> 00:46:20,624
Selcan Hatun and all our guests...

361
00:46:20,952 --> 00:46:24,952
they'll be neighbors of our prophet.

362
00:46:25,340 --> 00:46:29,340
Amin, my sheik.
Amin.

363
00:46:31,275 --> 00:46:36,075
Our tribe grew with suffering.

364
00:46:36,937 --> 00:46:42,247
As we fight the heathens with
a weapon on one hand...

365
00:46:42,674 --> 00:46:47,124
we buried our martyrs with
the other hand.

366
00:46:48,500 --> 00:46:52,110
It will always be like this.

367
00:46:53,535 --> 00:46:56,885
We know well that...

368
00:46:56,885 --> 00:47:02,135
the only thing they want...

369
00:47:02,903 --> 00:47:06,463
it to continue the cause
they died for.

370
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:12,000
I swear on our martyrs that...

371
00:47:12,000 --> 00:47:16,000
with Allah's approval we'll continue
this cause forever.

372
00:47:16,566 --> 00:47:19,166
Amin.

373
00:47:20,890 --> 00:47:24,890
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come in, Aygül.

374
00:47:35,300 --> 00:47:39,300
My bey, our scouts returned.
I wanted to inform you.

375
00:47:39,444 --> 00:47:42,454
The group that'll get Holafira
is on the way.

376
00:47:42,654 --> 00:47:44,974
Good.
Good.

377
00:47:45,019 --> 00:47:49,019
Keep the cautions high.

378
00:47:49,019 --> 00:47:53,019
Holofira is under our protection.
She should be safe.

379
00:47:53,019 --> 00:47:57,409
-Alps keep their eyes on her, my bey.
-Thank you.

380
00:47:57,409 --> 00:47:59,289
Thank you.

381
00:48:02,537 --> 00:48:05,277
Aygül.

382
00:48:06,666 --> 00:48:12,056
We waited for you at iftar but
we know how you feel.

383
00:48:12,056 --> 00:48:16,456
-We didn't want to disturb you.
-I know.

384
00:48:16,507 --> 00:48:19,507
Thank you, Bala.

385
00:48:23,206 --> 00:48:28,626
But the pain is so new.
I'll look for her at the iftar...

386
00:48:32,824 --> 00:48:36,824
Of course, you'll feel the
pain, my daughter.

387
00:48:36,824 --> 00:48:40,324
separation burns your heart.
I know it.

388
00:48:41,233 --> 00:48:45,233
But this separation isn't forever.

389
00:48:45,397 --> 00:48:49,397
The eternal home is waiting
for us.

390
00:48:50,554 --> 00:48:55,234
Our prophet lived for 63 years
in this world.

391
00:48:55,234 --> 00:49:00,214
So, we shouldn't be sad about death.
We should always remember the dead.

392
00:49:00,214 --> 00:49:05,974
And keep their place fresh with
prayers and Qur-an.

393
00:49:07,332 --> 00:49:11,332
When you reunite in the afterlife...

394
00:49:11,332 --> 00:49:14,942
it'll feel like you were never
separated.

395
00:49:16,158 --> 00:49:20,158
Come on, sit with us.

396
00:49:59,906 --> 00:50:03,906
We need extra caution
on the way back.

397
00:50:03,906 --> 00:50:07,906
Rest well now. After getting Holofira,
no one will blink.

398
00:50:08,043 --> 00:50:12,043
Don't worry, Alexander. We'll
get Holofira to her aunt safely.

399
00:50:47,697 --> 00:50:52,287
As you ordered, their uniforms
aren't damaged, sir.

400
00:50:53,684 --> 00:50:57,084
Very well done.

401
00:51:01,674 --> 00:51:06,304
I don't want any mistakes.
You'll go to Kayı Tribe.

402
00:51:06,669 --> 00:51:11,129
-And you'll get Holofira.
-Be at ease, sir.

403
00:51:11,129 --> 00:51:15,129
-We remember every word.
-Good.

404
00:51:27,174 --> 00:51:32,214
You are finally awakened.
You are alive for now.

405
00:51:34,963 --> 00:51:38,963
You'll regret not killing me, Osman Bey.

406
00:51:40,530 --> 00:51:43,600
Everything has a time.

407
00:51:44,968 --> 00:51:48,968
You are a very smart man.

408
00:51:50,052 --> 00:51:55,182
You'll use me as a card. But
it's in vain.

409
00:51:56,465 --> 00:52:01,275
No one will give you anything
for me.

410
00:52:01,753 --> 00:52:05,753
Especially İnegöl.

411
00:52:06,211 --> 00:52:10,211
Do you think that you can get
İnegöl in return for me?

412
00:52:10,300 --> 00:52:15,310
Now is not the time to ask questions
but to answer them.

413
00:52:18,732 --> 00:52:23,952
Say it. Who are you working with?

414
00:52:26,063 --> 00:52:29,373
You are asking Master Darius.

415
00:52:29,373 --> 00:52:33,373
You'll see who he is, only
when you feel...

416
00:52:33,373 --> 00:52:36,643
his sword upon your neck.

417
00:52:38,715 --> 00:52:42,715
By the way, Davud...

418
00:52:42,715 --> 00:52:45,525
Davud the Smith, yes.

419
00:52:46,905 --> 00:52:53,625
I wounded him badly. He made a lot of
noise. He must be dead already.

420
00:52:54,456 --> 00:52:58,456
Master Davud is alive.
He'll be better.

421
00:53:00,796 --> 00:53:04,796
-But you--
-Let him be alive, Osman Bey.

422
00:53:04,970 --> 00:53:10,370
Let him live. I took so much
from you.

423
00:53:12,122 --> 00:53:15,122
I took your alps.

424
00:53:15,605 --> 00:53:19,605
I took your women, children...

425
00:53:19,605 --> 00:53:22,565
I took your loved ones.

426
00:53:23,893 --> 00:53:28,433
I took your beloved brother Savcı.

427
00:53:30,035 --> 00:53:34,445
I won't leave a single person
around you. I'll take them all!

428
00:53:34,445 --> 00:53:39,725
What can you do to me?
You can kill me at most.

429
00:53:40,605 --> 00:53:44,605
Go on and take it.
Take my life.

430
00:53:44,727 --> 00:53:47,047
Is that so?

431
00:54:07,986 --> 00:54:12,786
You can't take anything from me.

432
00:54:14,720 --> 00:54:18,720
Those who fall for the
right path...

433
00:54:18,720 --> 00:54:22,720
get rewarded with heaven.

434
00:54:22,720 --> 00:54:26,720
You can't take anything from me.

435
00:54:28,653 --> 00:54:32,653
The one who has the will of steel,
doesn't get affected by anything.

436
00:54:34,231 --> 00:54:38,931
Your intention is to play with my
anger and get yourself killed.

437
00:54:41,575 --> 00:54:45,575
You want to kill yourself to
save İnegöl.

438
00:54:46,695 --> 00:54:49,855
Your bravery won't work on me...

439
00:54:51,251 --> 00:54:54,621
and I won't lose to my anger.

440
00:55:09,845 --> 00:55:12,875
Either you live or die...

441
00:55:14,700 --> 00:55:17,290
I'll take İnegöl.

442
00:55:22,106 --> 00:55:27,726
Either I live or die, I won't give
you İnegöl!

443
00:55:33,034 --> 00:55:35,694
Oh, my beautiful mother.

444
00:55:37,248 --> 00:55:42,268
She was a mother to us all.
All of this tribe.

445
00:55:43,276 --> 00:55:46,456
She loved you a lot, Olofira.

446
00:55:46,456 --> 00:55:49,806
I loved her too.

447
00:55:52,623 --> 00:55:56,623
You too. I love all of you.

448
00:55:56,623 --> 00:55:59,893
You are so different.

449
00:56:01,024 --> 00:56:06,154
What's different about us?
Come, tell me.

450
00:56:07,613 --> 00:56:09,693
Everything.

451
00:56:10,664 --> 00:56:14,664
Where you live, where
you sleep.

452
00:56:15,557 --> 00:56:20,107
Then, the river, the tents...

453
00:56:24,141 --> 00:56:27,711
no children can feel like they
are in a cage.

454
00:56:31,390 --> 00:56:34,050
My pretty girl.

455
00:56:36,962 --> 00:56:40,962
You won't feel like you
are in a cage again.

456
00:56:40,962 --> 00:56:44,962
If that cage is a dungeon for you,
then you won't go there.

457
00:57:20,246 --> 00:57:24,246
Come on, Alahaddin.
Don't think that much.

458
00:57:24,358 --> 00:57:28,358
You rush for everything, brother.
Be patient.

459
00:57:28,461 --> 00:57:32,721
-To make the right move, I must think.
-No.

460
00:57:32,721 --> 00:57:36,161
For the right move, you need
to act fast.

461
00:57:36,161 --> 00:57:40,051
Without wasting time,
you'll grab the enemy's throat!

462
00:57:56,541 --> 00:58:00,931
That's through for battle, brother.
But rushing in this game...

463
00:58:00,931 --> 00:58:03,721
makes you lose it.

464
00:58:04,527 --> 00:58:08,317
I'll beat you and show you
what makes you lose it.

465
00:58:13,599 --> 00:58:17,599
Alahaddin, do they play
this game...

466
00:58:17,599 --> 00:58:21,949
in İznik, Bursa,
Constantinople?

467
00:58:24,442 --> 00:58:28,672
I don't know. Holofira knows though.

468
00:58:28,672 --> 00:58:33,492
-Her aunt lives there.
-Right. Holofira knows it.

469
00:58:36,107 --> 00:58:39,387
I wonder how is it like there.

470
00:58:40,508 --> 00:58:43,248
Constantinople.

471
00:58:43,577 --> 00:58:47,577
Brother, one day, I'll go there.

472
00:58:56,564 --> 00:59:00,564
Attacking from here isn't reasonable.

473
00:59:00,564 --> 00:59:04,564
We've been hearing it.
Nikola strengthened his walls.

474
00:59:06,783 --> 00:59:11,403
You are right, Gündüz Bey. But that's
the shortest way to the inner castle.

475
00:59:11,836 --> 00:59:16,916
If we enter from a single front, we'll
get stuck. We'll have high casualties.

476
00:59:17,868 --> 00:59:22,138
Gündüz Bey. Turgut Bey is right.

477
00:59:24,285 --> 00:59:28,285
We shouldn't have high casualties.
If needed...

478
00:59:28,285 --> 00:59:32,995
we can hit the walls for weeks.
But we don't know what to expect inside.

479
00:59:35,758 --> 00:59:38,818
I said it's not reasonable, Konur.

480
00:59:42,046 --> 00:59:45,406
I didn't say it's impossible.

481
00:59:46,706 --> 00:59:50,716
Let's wait for Osman Bey and
see what he says.

482
00:59:51,195 --> 00:59:54,565
Behold! Osman Bey!

483
00:59:57,997 --> 01:00:02,347
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

484
01:00:11,024 --> 01:00:15,844
We were tasked with the campaign,
not the victory.

485
01:00:16,897 --> 01:00:20,897
But many gratitudes to my mighty
Allah that...

486
01:00:20,897 --> 01:00:24,897
we were destined for victory.

487
01:00:25,800 --> 01:00:28,570
Bilecik Castle is ours.

488
01:00:28,570 --> 01:00:32,900
Now, İnegöl Castle is
our target.

489
01:00:35,745 --> 01:00:39,165
We have Nikola now.

490
01:00:41,544 --> 01:00:45,544
And he values the castle
over his life.

491
01:00:45,822 --> 01:00:51,032
He'll do anything to stop
the exchange.

492
01:00:53,514 --> 01:00:56,424
We'll siege the castle.

493
01:00:58,583 --> 01:01:01,753
We can siege the castle, my bey.

494
01:01:01,753 --> 01:01:05,753
We'll cut the lines of supply too.

495
01:01:07,127 --> 01:01:12,167
But we have no catapults to hit the walls
or battering rams to break the gate.

496
01:01:14,515 --> 01:01:19,545
My bey, this will be a long siege.

497
01:01:20,411 --> 01:01:25,201
Also, we'll suffer the reinforcements
of the emperor and the other lords.

498
01:01:25,989 --> 01:01:28,779
We can cut the support lines.

499
01:01:29,651 --> 01:01:34,761
But if they come for a battle,
we'll be in the open no matter what.

500
01:01:36,043 --> 01:01:39,583
It'll be as you said.

501
01:01:39,910 --> 01:01:43,650
We'll cut the supply lines.

502
01:01:43,650 --> 01:01:48,440
We'll put scouts on all sides
of the castle.

503
01:01:49,429 --> 01:01:54,069
And not a single reinforcement will
reach İnegöl.

504
01:01:55,090 --> 01:01:59,090
We'll do all this in a very
short time.

505
01:01:59,541 --> 01:02:02,861
It'll be over in a day.

506
01:02:08,061 --> 01:02:12,061
The place where they burned...

507
01:02:12,061 --> 01:02:15,341
was where the weapons
were being built.

508
01:02:20,414 --> 01:02:24,014
But not where they are kept.

509
01:02:24,649 --> 01:02:29,419
We hid the ammunition with
Cerkutay's trade...

510
01:02:30,801 --> 01:02:34,801
and took them to every corner
of İnegöl.

511
01:02:36,829 --> 01:02:42,429
The ladders are here,
the catapults are here...

512
01:02:45,116 --> 01:02:49,116
the battering ram is here.

513
01:02:50,836 --> 01:02:55,506
So, the war was in İnegöl
for years.

514
01:02:56,050 --> 01:02:59,580
But they didn't know it.

515
01:03:01,582 --> 01:03:06,582
Forgive us, Osman Bey. But when
were we going to hear this?

516
01:03:08,759 --> 01:03:12,759
A secret is a burden, Turgut Bey.

517
01:03:13,864 --> 01:03:18,184
But don't think that I don't
trust you.

518
01:03:19,692 --> 01:03:24,292
-I was capable of carrying it. So I did.
-Thank you.

519
01:03:26,088 --> 01:03:31,018
Now, you know it.
There is more.

520
01:03:33,122 --> 01:03:37,982
Master Davud was working on the
bursting cannon balls of Akça Çoban.

521
01:03:38,767 --> 01:03:41,887
He succeeded.

522
01:03:41,887 --> 01:03:45,887
And we placed them around İnegöl.

523
01:03:46,635 --> 01:03:51,935
The old man was working on it for
a long time. It's the best time to finish.

524
01:03:53,114 --> 01:03:58,654
Now, they don't think that we have
the weapons for a siege.

525
01:03:59,371 --> 01:04:03,911
When they see us, I pity them.

526
01:04:03,911 --> 01:04:07,941
True. True, brother.

527
01:04:08,856 --> 01:04:13,446
It's your task to build the
catapults and start the siege.

528
01:04:15,037 --> 01:04:18,337
Be on your way soon.

529
01:04:18,337 --> 01:04:22,337
As Master Davud said,
''Tomorrow...

530
01:04:23,761 --> 01:04:26,961
we'll be hitting the walls of
İnegöl.''

531
01:04:27,318 --> 01:04:30,748
-Inshallah.
-Inshallah, my bey.

532
01:04:33,304 --> 01:04:36,994
Now is time for conquest.

533
01:04:53,823 --> 01:04:56,173
O' the healer!

534
01:04:57,080 --> 01:05:02,630
Bring down your grace for
your subject, Koses.

535
01:05:03,037 --> 01:05:07,037
Heal him.

536
01:05:07,037 --> 01:05:12,407
For the sake of your
prophet Muhammed.

537
01:05:14,406 --> 01:05:19,456
For the sake of your proper
Jesus.

538
01:05:20,678 --> 01:05:24,868
Heal the wounds of this
wounded subject.

539
01:05:24,868 --> 01:05:29,278
Heal him, my Allah.

540
01:05:30,386 --> 01:05:33,756
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

541
01:05:34,288 --> 01:05:51,044
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

542
01:05:51,142 --> 01:05:52,812
Allahu Akbar!

543
01:05:52,812 --> 01:06:04,613
-There is no God but Allah!
-Allahu Akbar!

544
01:06:50,527 --> 01:06:52,757
Osman Bey!

545
01:06:53,294 --> 01:06:57,294
-What happened, Barkın Bey?
-It's not good!

546
01:06:57,294 --> 01:07:01,294
Selvi, my people, they are all
in danger! Help us!

547
01:07:01,294 --> 01:07:03,804
I need your help!

548
01:07:03,804 --> 01:07:08,184
-Who did this?
-That dog Romanus!

549
01:07:08,184 --> 01:07:12,354
He captured Selvi and my people
on their way to the upland.

550
01:07:12,354 --> 01:07:16,744
-In return...
-He wants Nikola in return.

551
01:07:17,454 --> 01:07:20,864
But not only Nikola.

552
01:07:21,420 --> 01:07:25,480
He wants the soldiers you
captured in Bilecik Castle.

553
01:07:25,480 --> 01:07:29,750
If we don't release them, he says
that he'll kill them all.

554
01:07:29,750 --> 01:07:34,160
For Allah's sake,
help us, Osman Bey.

555
01:07:35,451 --> 01:07:38,671
If something happens to my Selvi,
to my people...

556
01:07:39,405 --> 01:07:44,285
Don't worry, Barkın Bey. when did
we ever leave someone behind?

557
01:07:47,368 --> 01:07:52,158
But, there were going to leave
secretly.

558
01:07:55,178 --> 01:07:59,178
Who told the destination?

559
01:07:59,609 --> 01:08:03,609
We have no other chance to
save Nikola, Barkın.

560
01:08:03,609 --> 01:08:08,829
On the way to the upland, we'll capture
Selvi and the tribespeople.

561
01:08:08,829 --> 01:08:12,609
-In return for Nikola--
-No!

562
01:08:13,227 --> 01:08:17,617
I won't let you take Selvi.
Take anyone from the tribe.

563
01:08:17,617 --> 01:08:21,787
-But not Selvi!
-Barkın. Don't worry.

564
01:08:21,787 --> 01:08:26,087
It's just a game. I promise you.

565
01:08:26,087 --> 01:08:29,277
Selvi won't get hurt.

566
01:08:30,794 --> 01:08:35,144
As we talked, Osman Bey.
I didn't tell it to anyone.

567
01:08:35,144 --> 01:08:38,694
They knew it before you left.

568
01:08:41,163 --> 01:08:46,014
We'll find that out later.

569
01:08:46,015 --> 01:08:50,015
But we should think about
what we'll do now.

570
01:08:50,337 --> 01:08:53,868
Barkın! Barkın!

571
01:08:53,886 --> 01:08:58,006
Where is Selvi? What's happening,
Osman Bey? Is it true?

572
01:08:59,073 --> 01:09:04,504
It is, Malhun Hatun. But we'll save Selvi
before they hurt her.

573
01:09:05,420 --> 01:09:08,149
Right, Osman Bey?

574
01:09:10,344 --> 01:09:14,613
We won't leave my sister
to those tyrants, right?

575
01:09:14,790 --> 01:09:20,100
Malhun, be at ease. We'll save Selvi.

576
01:09:20,100 --> 01:09:23,260
When did we ever leave someone
behind, my bey?

577
01:09:27,524 --> 01:09:29,705
True.

578
01:09:30,776 --> 01:09:34,106
We won't Selvi to them.

579
01:09:47,551 --> 01:09:52,140
Look at this smell.
It smells awful.

580
01:09:52,689 --> 01:09:57,259
Disgusting shepherd tent.
Disgusting.

581
01:09:57,910 --> 01:10:01,910
Be happy that I didn't
put you next to the snakes.

582
01:10:05,536 --> 01:10:07,276
You'll go to your castle now.

583
01:10:09,984 --> 01:10:12,084
To my castle?

584
01:10:13,708 --> 01:10:16,108
Are you letting me?

585
01:10:17,461 --> 01:10:19,121
You?

586
01:10:20,241 --> 01:10:21,951
Osman Bey.

587
01:10:23,718 --> 01:10:28,618
What made you change your mind,
Osman Bey?

588
01:10:34,433 --> 01:10:37,603
As I can understand from your silence...

589
01:10:38,139 --> 01:10:41,009
...you couldn't get what you wanted.

590
01:10:43,875 --> 01:10:48,415
I was not intended to stay
in that tent either.

591
01:10:48,889 --> 01:10:50,779
I was going to leave.

592
01:10:56,761 --> 01:10:58,501
Good.

593
01:10:59,559 --> 01:11:01,779
You should know that...

594
01:11:02,216 --> 01:11:07,096
...I will not let you sleep in that
comfy bed in your castle.

595
01:11:08,714 --> 01:11:10,824
You will fear me...

596
01:11:13,617 --> 01:11:17,057
You wonder when I will show up
and kill you.

597
01:11:19,273 --> 01:11:22,553
You won't be able to sleep.

598
01:11:29,723 --> 01:11:31,323
Untie him.

599
01:11:39,177 --> 01:11:41,457
You barbarians!

600
01:12:57,204 --> 01:12:59,364
Hey people!

601
01:13:11,089 --> 01:13:13,929
I want to kill that ignoble...

602
01:13:14,995 --> 01:13:17,325
...the most.

603
01:13:21,339 --> 01:13:22,839
But...

604
01:13:24,674 --> 01:13:27,134
Selvi Hatun...

605
01:13:27,340 --> 01:13:30,150
...and Barkin Bey's people
are captivated.

606
01:13:35,281 --> 01:13:38,751
If the people there gets hurt...

607
01:13:40,022 --> 01:13:43,862
...because of this dog...

608
01:13:45,200 --> 01:13:47,740
...I cannot forgive myself.

609
01:13:49,894 --> 01:13:52,204
Now you tell me!

610
01:13:53,079 --> 01:13:55,029
Can you forgive yourself...

611
01:13:57,621 --> 01:14:00,291
...if they kill our people there...

612
01:14:01,825 --> 01:14:04,935
...because of this infidel?

613
01:14:06,345 --> 01:14:08,365
Tell me!

614
01:14:13,320 --> 01:14:16,170
That ignoble martyred my son.

615
01:14:16,495 --> 01:14:19,095
He burned my heart!

616
01:14:19,660 --> 01:14:22,880
But you are right.

617
01:14:23,091 --> 01:14:25,951
Others shouldn't suffer anymore.

618
01:14:26,419 --> 01:14:29,779
We will wait for our revenge.

619
01:14:38,499 --> 01:14:40,829
Don't worry.

620
01:14:42,137 --> 01:14:44,117
Don't worry at all.

621
01:14:44,439 --> 01:14:46,129
They will not last long.

622
01:14:47,377 --> 01:14:49,827
I swear on the martyrs!

623
01:14:55,346 --> 01:14:58,326
I am going to kill Nikola myself.

624
01:15:02,800 --> 01:15:03,810
But...

625
01:15:07,600 --> 01:15:09,930
...he'll go for the swap now.

626
01:15:18,605 --> 01:15:20,565
Turgut Bey.

627
01:15:24,333 --> 01:15:26,463
I assign you with this important duty.

628
01:15:27,288 --> 01:15:30,578
Bring Selvi Hatun and Barkin Bey's people
safe and sound.

629
01:15:31,560 --> 01:15:35,710
As you say, Osman Bey.
We won't let those dogs play a trick on us.

630
01:15:37,395 --> 01:15:39,595
- Kutan!
- My Bey!

631
01:15:42,824 --> 01:15:44,534
He laughs.

632
01:15:53,566 --> 01:15:56,226
No power could get you out of
this tribe alive...

633
01:15:56,400 --> 01:15:59,620
...if you were more important than
our people.

634
01:15:59,706 --> 01:16:01,286
Come on!

635
01:16:14,450 --> 01:16:16,590
Come on!

636
01:16:32,759 --> 01:16:34,209
So, my Bey.

637
01:16:34,668 --> 01:16:36,768
What's next?

638
01:16:37,886 --> 01:16:38,986
What will we do?

639
01:16:39,570 --> 01:16:40,910
We won't stop.

640
01:16:42,174 --> 01:16:44,214
If they play a trick on us...

641
01:16:44,569 --> 01:16:46,759
...we'll set up a trick as well.

642
01:16:51,520 --> 01:16:52,690
Let's go!

643
01:17:31,010 --> 01:17:34,310
We will cut all the branches Osman holds.

644
01:17:35,287 --> 01:17:38,757
None will get out of that mine alive!

645
01:17:39,705 --> 01:17:42,295
We will first claim that mine...

646
01:17:43,013 --> 01:17:47,423
...then we will blow that mine up.

647
01:17:51,154 --> 01:17:52,676
Is the Greek fire ready?

648
01:17:52,676 --> 01:17:55,416
Everything is just as you command, sir.

649
01:17:56,074 --> 01:17:57,764
Good.

650
01:17:58,271 --> 01:17:59,651
Good.

651
01:18:05,104 --> 01:18:07,954
- Good luck, Hatuns.
- Thank you Ayse Hatun.

652
01:18:08,152 --> 01:18:11,452
Hay Masha Allah!
Hay Masha Allah!

653
01:18:12,379 --> 01:18:14,699
- Good luck!
- Thank you!

654
01:18:15,610 --> 01:18:17,340
Hatuns!

655
01:18:18,645 --> 01:18:21,375
Inegol preparations are on!

656
01:18:21,481 --> 01:18:24,381
From now on, we'll work for the war.

657
01:18:24,776 --> 01:18:27,606
You'll give a break to weaving rugs.

658
01:18:28,985 --> 01:18:33,125
Ayse Hatun, distribution of the swords
is your responsibility.

659
01:18:33,509 --> 01:18:36,440
You'll produce arrows and shields
with Hatuns.

660
01:18:36,440 --> 01:18:38,760
People from Ahis will come to help you.

661
01:18:38,928 --> 01:18:41,328
Don't worry, Malhun.

662
01:18:41,491 --> 01:18:45,331
Our Alps will have no lackings
with Allah's permit.

663
01:18:45,663 --> 01:18:47,553
Thank Allah.

664
01:18:48,348 --> 01:18:52,538
Alaca, you and hatuns will take care of
Alps' food.

665
01:18:52,706 --> 01:18:54,548
We don't know how long this war last.

666
01:18:54,548 --> 01:18:56,983
So work hard.

667
01:18:56,983 --> 01:18:59,063
As you command, Malhun Hatun.

668
01:19:00,901 --> 01:19:02,741
Kumral Abdal!

669
01:19:03,273 --> 01:19:05,023
How is the healing house?

670
01:19:08,902 --> 01:19:11,740
We allocated the tents near
the healing house...

671
01:19:11,740 --> 01:19:13,770
...to wounded Alps.

672
01:19:14,141 --> 01:19:15,772
Alps are getting the tents ready.

673
01:19:15,772 --> 01:19:20,082
Thank Allah, we have enough herbs...

674
01:19:20,187 --> 01:19:21,483
...and remedies.

675
01:19:21,483 --> 01:19:23,183
Thank Allah.

676
01:19:23,183 --> 01:19:26,481
Aydogdu and hatuns will be responsible
of wounded Alps.

677
01:19:26,481 --> 01:19:30,685
Hatuns, go with Kumral Abdal.
Take what you need.

678
01:19:30,685 --> 01:19:32,245
Have no shortage.

679
01:19:33,736 --> 01:19:35,876
The war has come!

680
01:19:36,678 --> 01:19:41,378
Our Alps and sisters will sweat on
battlefield, we will work here!

681
01:19:41,780 --> 01:19:45,370
Come on!
Kayi needs your service!

682
01:19:49,804 --> 01:19:51,804
Let's do it Hatuns!

683
01:19:56,560 --> 01:19:57,650
Up!

684
01:19:57,979 --> 01:19:59,199
Wait!

685
01:19:59,249 --> 01:20:00,269
Duck!

686
01:20:00,491 --> 01:20:02,291
Faster!
Shoot!

687
01:20:04,432 --> 01:20:06,732
Up!
Wait!

688
01:20:07,131 --> 01:20:08,479
Duck!

689
01:20:08,479 --> 01:20:09,939
Shoot!

690
01:20:11,078 --> 01:20:12,658
Up!

691
01:20:12,763 --> 01:20:14,143
Wait!

692
01:20:14,442 --> 01:20:16,092
Duck!

693
01:20:16,414 --> 01:20:17,924
Shoot!

694
01:20:19,126 --> 01:20:20,306
Up!

695
01:20:20,414 --> 01:20:21,634
Wait!

696
01:20:22,197 --> 01:20:23,787
Duck!

697
01:20:24,422 --> 01:20:25,982
Shoot!

698
01:20:28,103 --> 01:20:29,763
Up!

699
01:20:30,511 --> 01:20:31,841
Wait!

700
01:20:31,894 --> 01:20:33,324
Duck!

701
01:20:33,693 --> 01:20:35,233
What is the situation, Aygul?

702
01:20:36,913 --> 01:20:38,833
Masha Allah(praise be) to them, Bala!

703
01:20:38,888 --> 01:20:40,838
You trained them well.

704
01:20:42,603 --> 01:20:45,143
It is obvious that they learned from you.

705
01:20:48,977 --> 01:20:51,817
The rest of the sisters
are busy helping Hatuns.

706
01:20:55,312 --> 01:20:57,802
The rest of them needs more training.

707
01:21:00,076 --> 01:21:01,586
Good.

708
01:21:03,249 --> 01:21:05,149
Sisters!

709
01:21:11,560 --> 01:21:13,520
My valiant Hatuns!

710
01:21:17,609 --> 01:21:21,829
You proved your skills in
every fight you enganged.

711
01:21:22,684 --> 01:21:25,304
We are proud of you.
Thank you.

712
01:21:28,297 --> 01:21:30,137
Aygül Hatun?

713
01:21:30,668 --> 01:21:32,048
What do you think?

714
01:21:32,762 --> 01:21:35,582
Are the sisters ready for a new war?

715
01:21:36,766 --> 01:21:40,746
Even the most naive sisters are now
ready for the war.

716
01:21:43,016 --> 01:21:45,206
They shoot the target in the first shoot.

717
01:21:46,473 --> 01:21:48,123
Masha Allah.

718
01:21:48,484 --> 01:21:50,324
Masha Allah!
(praise be!)

719
01:21:57,179 --> 01:22:00,439
What is the three rule of...

720
01:22:01,347 --> 01:22:02,416
...sisters?

721
01:22:02,416 --> 01:22:05,486
Take care of your job,
your family and your food!

722
01:22:06,251 --> 01:22:08,281
Hay Masha Allah!

723
01:22:10,756 --> 01:22:14,136
It is time for war!

724
01:22:21,743 --> 01:22:24,273
Our destination is Inegol!

725
01:22:24,964 --> 01:22:29,394
Sisters will not stop until...

726
01:22:29,897 --> 01:22:32,397
...we raise Kayi flags
on the Inegol walls!

727
01:22:33,556 --> 01:22:35,576
May our fight be holy!

728
01:22:36,306 --> 01:22:58,266
Allah is the greatest!

729
01:23:17,021 --> 01:23:18,831
I am not going to kill you now.

730
01:23:19,831 --> 01:23:22,021
We have things to see.

731
01:23:23,869 --> 01:23:27,089
Turgut Bey, ah Turgut Bey.

732
01:23:28,285 --> 01:23:31,655
You should have killed me
when you caught me.

733
01:23:33,034 --> 01:23:36,254
Unfortunately, you failed to do so.

734
01:23:43,230 --> 01:23:44,970
What are you laughing at?

735
01:23:45,230 --> 01:23:47,680
Are you bored of living?

736
01:23:49,220 --> 01:23:51,190
Let me tell you this.

737
01:23:51,671 --> 01:23:54,721
He laughs longest who laughs last

738
01:23:58,147 --> 01:24:00,837
Selvi!
Selvi I'll save you!

739
01:24:01,416 --> 01:24:03,336
Stop Barkin Bey.

740
01:24:04,213 --> 01:24:06,673
We are here to get them
safe and sound.

741
01:24:10,764 --> 01:24:12,644
Turks!

742
01:24:13,391 --> 01:24:16,111
I am seeking opportunity to kill you.

743
01:24:17,689 --> 01:24:19,689
Let it be a clear swap.

744
01:24:23,036 --> 01:24:24,716
Otherwise...

745
01:24:26,368 --> 01:24:29,038
I'll kill the captives first...

746
01:24:31,195 --> 01:24:33,925
...then I'll kill you!

747
01:24:34,963 --> 01:24:38,323
If you bark at Turks like that again,
I'll put a collar on your neck!

748
01:24:40,458 --> 01:24:42,628
Of course the swap will be clear.

749
01:24:43,844 --> 01:24:48,044
There's a idiom that you don't know.
Our words are our honor.

750
01:24:50,176 --> 01:24:54,086
Turgut Bey is right.
We need a clear swap too, Romanos.

751
01:24:55,621 --> 01:24:57,611
Free the captives now.

752
01:24:58,345 --> 01:25:01,615
-Nikola!
-Romanos.

753
01:25:01,929 --> 01:25:03,579
You are still breathing.

754
01:25:03,627 --> 01:25:05,987
I have seen better days.

755
01:25:06,925 --> 01:25:09,375
I want to return to my castle at once!

756
01:25:09,819 --> 01:25:13,469
Because I will end Turks.

757
01:25:17,809 --> 01:25:20,019
Why hurry?

758
01:25:20,651 --> 01:25:22,701
You will get away from us...

759
01:25:23,166 --> 01:25:25,156
...but you'll be close to the
grim reaper.

760
01:25:26,669 --> 01:25:28,329
You are not long for this world.

761
01:25:36,752 --> 01:25:38,402
Samil!

762
01:25:38,588 --> 01:25:40,168
Yes my Bey.

763
01:25:40,252 --> 01:25:43,279
We are always in a fight
since you came.

764
01:25:43,279 --> 01:25:45,259
Thank Allah, my Bey.

765
01:25:47,988 --> 01:25:51,609
Turan, Gencebey, Samil.

766
01:25:52,279 --> 01:25:54,779
You go at this direction.

767
01:25:54,796 --> 01:25:57,126
- As you command, my Bey.
- Eyvallah (thank you).

768
01:25:57,794 --> 01:26:01,000
Boran, Cerkutay, you'll join me.

769
01:26:01,000 --> 01:26:03,760
- Eyvallah (yes) my Bey
- Eyvallah (yes) my Bey

770
01:26:04,500 --> 01:26:06,440
You know what to do.

771
01:26:06,695 --> 01:26:08,755
I want no hitch.

772
01:26:09,083 --> 01:26:11,253
We'll reveal the truth.

773
01:26:11,419 --> 01:26:13,769
Let's go
May our fight be blessed!

774
01:26:13,854 --> 01:26:15,214
- Amen
- Amen.

775
01:26:15,214 --> 01:26:16,214
Let's go valiants.

776
01:26:21,886 --> 01:26:23,666
I will send the captives!

777
01:26:24,240 --> 01:26:28,930
Send Nikola and the rest
at the same time.

778
01:26:30,055 --> 01:26:31,714
Come on.

779
01:26:31,714 --> 01:26:33,684
- Kutan
- My Bey.

780
01:26:44,780 --> 01:26:46,720
Let's do it.

781
01:27:34,466 --> 01:27:36,346
Come, brothers.

782
01:27:36,461 --> 01:27:37,721
Come.

783
01:27:49,259 --> 01:27:50,989
Selvi!

784
01:27:52,699 --> 01:27:54,969
Okay, easy.

785
01:27:58,372 --> 01:28:00,828
I was so afraid, Barkin.
I was so afraid.

786
01:28:00,828 --> 01:28:03,818
It's over.
It's all over.

787
01:28:03,881 --> 01:28:05,541
Let's go.

788
01:28:07,343 --> 01:28:09,153
Turgut Bey!

789
01:28:13,591 --> 01:28:15,301
Nikola!

790
01:28:25,261 --> 01:28:26,781
Soldier!

791
01:28:32,680 --> 01:28:34,000
Where is Vasilius?

792
01:28:34,611 --> 01:28:36,271
He is dead.

793
01:28:36,432 --> 01:28:38,072
Turks buried him.

794
01:28:41,387 --> 01:28:44,267
Another reason to burn their tribe.

795
01:28:46,199 --> 01:28:49,539
But I'll wait for Arius to
destroy the mines first.

796
01:28:56,206 --> 01:28:57,676
Turgut Bey.

797
01:28:57,878 --> 01:29:00,398
Alps.
Thank you.

798
01:29:00,664 --> 01:29:01,984
I appreciate this.

799
01:29:01,984 --> 01:29:04,481
- You are fine, right?
- Thank Allah, we are.

800
01:29:04,979 --> 01:29:06,789
Eyvallah (thank you) Turgut Bey.

801
01:29:07,340 --> 01:29:08,650
Eyvallah (sure).

802
01:29:12,208 --> 01:29:14,418
This Nikola got rid of me again!

803
01:29:15,324 --> 01:29:17,564
He did it again!

804
01:29:18,231 --> 01:29:19,871
It's enough!

805
01:29:20,410 --> 01:29:22,980
Not much left, Turgut Bey.

806
01:29:24,224 --> 01:29:26,874
He'll pay for the pain he gave.

807
01:29:29,542 --> 01:29:31,972
Not much left, Nikola.

808
01:29:48,612 --> 01:29:51,712
You won't have anything left
when you lose here, Osman.

809
01:29:55,238 --> 01:29:58,568
We are attacking now.
Kill them all.

810
01:29:58,850 --> 01:30:02,300
Imprison them all in the eternal darkness!

811
01:30:02,774 --> 01:30:04,244
Now!

812
01:30:09,459 --> 01:30:13,459
Let's show those dogs who the boss is.

813
01:30:14,049 --> 01:30:17,071
Brothers, blast the
wind of Caucasian on them!

814
01:30:17,071 --> 01:30:20,011
Let's break their tooth
one by one, brothers.

815
01:30:20,246 --> 01:30:22,686
My sword is out of patience.

816
01:30:25,411 --> 01:30:27,151
The infidel are riding for a fall!

817
01:31:18,518 --> 01:31:20,768
Where are you running, ha?

818
01:31:41,395 --> 01:31:43,775
How could you know we were here?

819
01:31:43,937 --> 01:31:45,957
How did you learn it?

820
01:31:46,501 --> 01:31:48,371
Coward dog.

821
01:31:50,741 --> 01:31:53,101
You are afraid to show your face.

822
01:31:54,380 --> 01:31:56,970
Yet you don't fear my wrath.

823
01:31:57,440 --> 01:31:58,440
Ha?

824
01:32:02,551 --> 01:32:04,061
Let's see.

825
01:32:23,048 --> 01:32:25,748
You came to my tent...

826
01:32:27,135 --> 01:32:29,335
...in guise of Fiqh (fiqh person).

827
01:32:30,317 --> 01:32:32,357
You ate my food.

828
01:32:33,110 --> 01:32:35,290
You were my guest!

829
01:32:36,105 --> 01:32:38,065
How did you catch me?

830
01:32:38,226 --> 01:32:39,666
How?

831
01:32:41,559 --> 01:32:43,539
You!

832
01:32:53,097 --> 01:32:55,017
You!

833
01:32:55,170 --> 01:32:58,830
You are a devil in guise of fiqh!

834
01:32:58,995 --> 01:33:04,085
But I am a wolf in guise of human!

835
01:33:06,531 --> 01:33:11,111
Now you are in my paws.

836
01:33:28,670 --> 01:33:30,850
Came from Aktemur, my Bey.

837
01:33:47,685 --> 01:33:50,535
Arius and Commander Romanus...

838
01:33:50,889 --> 01:33:53,709
...will claim the mines
and blow them up.

839
01:33:56,744 --> 01:34:01,834
They want to prevent us from conquering
Inegol by removing our source of ammunation.

840
01:34:05,451 --> 01:34:07,401
Good.

841
01:34:08,042 --> 01:34:09,792
Good.

842
01:34:10,192 --> 01:34:12,022
Let them come.

843
01:34:13,308 --> 01:34:16,728
Let them come and
witness our wrath!

844
01:34:20,750 --> 01:34:23,470
You'll be defeated by our darkness, Osman!

845
01:34:34,383 --> 01:34:36,163
You!

846
01:34:37,512 --> 01:34:40,402
You are a devil in disguise!

847
01:34:41,625 --> 01:34:46,955
You came in my tent.
You ate my food in my table.

848
01:34:49,246 --> 01:34:51,686
You tried to trick us with Quran!

849
01:34:54,283 --> 01:34:56,063
You!

850
01:34:57,521 --> 01:34:59,981
You have betrayed!

851
01:35:01,110 --> 01:35:02,550
You!

852
01:35:03,441 --> 01:35:08,131
You, so it was you behind it all!

853
01:35:15,822 --> 01:35:18,822
Come here!
You tried to lay Sogut at our door!

854
01:35:20,642 --> 01:35:22,502
Come!

855
01:35:22,714 --> 01:35:27,144
You killed Mari, Umur Bey, Ivaz Bey, huh?

856
01:35:30,002 --> 01:35:31,372
Come here.

857
01:35:32,418 --> 01:35:35,828
So you intended to kill Sheik Edebali.

858
01:35:36,039 --> 01:35:37,209
You!

859
01:35:38,103 --> 01:35:43,143
Sheik Edebali.
I made him both live and die.

860
01:35:43,805 --> 01:35:46,715
He lives thanks to me.

861
01:35:48,616 --> 01:35:51,585
Admit it, Osman.
How was my acting?

862
01:35:51,585 --> 01:35:53,455
I acted very well!

863
01:35:55,443 --> 01:35:59,323
I acted looking at you in the eye.

864
01:36:02,275 --> 01:36:06,045
We will always be there
and end you.

865
01:36:06,432 --> 01:36:08,922
We will end you Osman.

866
01:36:12,982 --> 01:36:14,802
You...

867
01:36:15,264 --> 01:36:17,764
...only end yourselves.

868
01:36:19,133 --> 01:36:21,973
So you have been evil for years, huh?

869
01:36:22,997 --> 01:36:25,747
You played many tricks behind us.

870
01:36:26,778 --> 01:36:31,518
But you managed nothing.

871
01:36:33,203 --> 01:36:37,113
I killed many cruels until now.

872
01:36:37,713 --> 01:36:40,573
Now look at me.

873
01:36:42,094 --> 01:36:44,624
These eyes are the last eyes you see!

874
01:36:45,436 --> 01:36:46,636
Last eyes!

875
01:36:49,877 --> 01:36:51,847
Your time is up.

876
01:38:38,675 --> 01:38:40,115
Selvi!

877
01:38:42,131 --> 01:38:46,061
Welcome, sister. Thank to the One who
let you meet us safe and sound.

878
01:38:46,452 --> 01:38:48,242
Thanks to Him, sister.

879
01:38:48,795 --> 01:38:50,855
Welcome Selvi Hatun.

880
01:38:51,980 --> 01:38:54,120
I don't know how to thank you.

881
01:38:54,803 --> 01:38:58,513
And Osman Bey.
How could he release Nikola?

882
01:38:59,225 --> 01:39:04,265
Osman Bey didn't think twice when it came
to the matter of our people's lives.

883
01:39:06,418 --> 01:39:07,928
Thank him.

884
01:39:08,341 --> 01:39:10,802
I was afraid to return empty handed...

885
01:39:10,802 --> 01:39:12,542
...while on my way to the tribe.

886
01:39:12,719 --> 01:39:16,276
But Osman Bey ignored his revenge...

887
01:39:16,516 --> 01:39:20,486
...gave up on Inegol castle
and saved you, Selvi.

888
01:39:21,979 --> 01:39:24,279
I owe Osman Bey a life.

889
01:39:24,597 --> 01:39:25,827
Thank him.

890
01:39:28,157 --> 01:39:30,867
Where is Osman Bey?
I couldn't see him.

891
01:39:44,393 --> 01:39:45,813
Sister.

892
01:39:46,129 --> 01:39:48,649
What is the preparations for?

893
01:39:48,859 --> 01:39:50,639
Preparation for conquest, sister.

894
01:39:51,303 --> 01:39:54,613
Osman Bey went to conquer Inegol.

895
01:39:56,710 --> 01:40:00,850
Hay Masha Allah.
Both Osman Bey and Kayi tribe won't stop!

896
01:40:03,570 --> 01:40:06,030
What we need to do is to help you.

897
01:40:07,778 --> 01:40:10,318
Kizilbeyoglu tribe Hatuns shall join you.

898
01:40:10,318 --> 01:40:13,282
Of course they can.
We need human power.

899
01:40:13,282 --> 01:40:15,943
We'll prepare for the war all together,
Insha Allah.

900
01:40:15,943 --> 01:40:17,873
Insha Allah (if Allah permits) sister.

901
01:40:18,578 --> 01:40:20,048
Insha Allah (if Allah permits)

902
01:40:42,376 --> 01:40:44,436
Did we receive the parts in Cobanpinar?

903
01:40:44,436 --> 01:40:46,166
We received them, my Bey.

904
01:40:52,454 --> 01:40:54,004
Yilanlik

905
01:40:54,256 --> 01:40:55,799
Hacilar.

906
01:40:55,799 --> 01:40:57,379
Yunusici.

907
01:40:57,800 --> 01:40:59,550
Baspinar.

908
01:40:59,752 --> 01:41:01,222
Yirce.

909
01:41:04,465 --> 01:41:06,165
It is now time to...

910
01:41:06,783 --> 01:41:11,583
...combine the catapults' each parts
of which we hided in different places.

911
01:41:11,629 --> 01:41:13,839
Eyvallah my Bey.

912
01:41:25,573 --> 01:41:32,363
Each part you carry contains
the blood and sweat of martyrs!

913
01:41:34,275 --> 01:41:38,195
For the sake of them, we will
destroy...

914
01:41:38,732 --> 01:41:42,142
...the walls of Inegol, Inshallah!

915
01:41:42,324 --> 01:41:44,294
Inshallah my Bey!

916
01:41:45,168 --> 01:41:46,788
Infidels martyred our valiants.

917
01:41:48,354 --> 01:41:52,634
They think they destroyed our ammo.

918
01:41:54,795 --> 01:41:57,195
But they couldn't manage.

919
01:41:58,508 --> 01:42:01,488
Praise be to Allah
The conquest has begun!

920
01:42:01,923 --> 01:42:03,077
The raid has begun!

921
01:42:03,077 --> 01:42:05,047
Praise be to Allah my Bey!

922
01:42:08,171 --> 01:42:10,292
Did we receive the catapults from
Papazik?

923
01:42:10,292 --> 01:42:13,112
We haven't yet, my Bey.
But we will soon, Inshallah.

924
01:42:15,198 --> 01:42:19,498
Come on then, valiants!
We'll start in the name of Allah!

925
01:42:21,283 --> 01:42:27,258
We will set up these catapults and
move them to Inegol walls!

926
01:42:27,258 --> 01:42:28,815
Inshallah my Bey!

927
01:42:28,815 --> 01:42:31,245
- In the name of Allah!
- In the name of Allah!

928
01:43:05,438 --> 01:43:08,458
Aya Nikola is back!

929
01:43:09,546 --> 01:43:14,116
Nobody, no single one can captivate me.

930
01:43:14,167 --> 01:43:15,637
They couldn't!

931
01:43:18,944 --> 01:43:20,744
Not only me.

932
01:43:20,851 --> 01:43:23,741
No one can claim my castle either.

933
01:43:23,825 --> 01:43:28,475
Only I, only Aya Nikola can rule it!

934
01:43:29,961 --> 01:43:34,211
I will remove whoever intends!

935
01:43:35,339 --> 01:43:36,979
Always remember!

936
01:43:37,931 --> 01:43:42,461
I am with you.
You are with me.

937
01:43:44,551 --> 01:43:49,531
Moreover, we have a great commander
who recently joined us.

938
01:43:51,337 --> 01:43:54,817
Commander Romanos!

939
01:43:56,822 --> 01:43:59,202
I thirst for blood!

940
01:44:00,924 --> 01:44:02,304
I..

941
01:44:03,589 --> 01:44:06,299
...and Aya Nikola will lead!

942
01:44:08,147 --> 01:44:12,467
And you will follow us, brave soldiers!

943
01:44:14,831 --> 01:44:17,861
- Are you with me?
- We are with you Aya Nikola!

944
01:44:18,236 --> 01:44:33,606
We are with you Commander Romanus!
We are with you Aya Nikola!

945
01:44:35,099 --> 01:44:38,479
I don't want any mistake.
You know what to do...

946
01:44:38,656 --> 01:44:40,386
...when you arrive in the tents.

947
01:44:40,386 --> 01:44:42,213
Don't worry, sir.

948
01:44:42,605 --> 01:44:45,825
Find me if you face any hitch.
Go now.

949
01:45:10,774 --> 01:45:16,004
I wish my mother had been here and seen
Hatuns who work without taking a breath.

950
01:45:16,477 --> 01:45:19,807
She would be very proud.
Right, Aygül?

951
01:45:19,950 --> 01:45:22,950
We don't have anyone to lead
us the way, Bala.

952
01:45:25,288 --> 01:45:26,578
It hurts...

953
01:45:27,613 --> 01:45:29,173
It hurts me the most...

954
01:45:29,982 --> 01:45:32,862
...that I wasn't there when
she took her last breath.

955
01:45:33,093 --> 01:45:34,573
Don't be sad, Aygül.

956
01:45:35,526 --> 01:45:38,476
Thank Allah she had no worries
when she died.

957
01:45:38,981 --> 01:45:43,141
She resigned her soul with peace.
We'll pray for her.

958
01:45:49,171 --> 01:45:52,711
Ah Mother Selcan.
She had been a mother for us too.

959
01:45:54,521 --> 01:45:56,941
It'll be hard to get used to
her absence.

960
01:45:57,792 --> 01:46:00,212
May Allah place her in heaven.

961
01:46:00,852 --> 01:46:02,402
Amen.

962
01:46:02,628 --> 01:46:04,128
Amen.

963
01:46:04,782 --> 01:46:06,982
Thank you Selvi Hatun.

964
01:46:10,509 --> 01:46:12,249
Ayse!

965
01:46:13,169 --> 01:46:15,480
Stop, don't do it by yourself.

966
01:46:15,480 --> 01:46:17,830
You are fasting.
You'll faint.

967
01:46:18,050 --> 01:46:21,230
I am doing nothing...

968
01:46:21,459 --> 01:46:23,849
...compared to what Alps and sisters
are doing.

969
01:46:25,201 --> 01:46:28,051
It is tiring, but it'll worth it.

970
01:46:30,262 --> 01:46:32,852
Peace be with your hearts, Hatuns!

971
01:46:33,891 --> 01:46:38,191
Do not tire yourself!
Do your job in turns. Have break!

972
01:46:42,686 --> 01:46:45,866
A Kayi Hatun doesn't have a break,
Bala Hatun!

973
01:46:48,161 --> 01:46:50,501
Hay Masha Allah, well said!

974
01:46:50,691 --> 01:46:53,981
We will work on and on
until we conquer Inegol.

975
01:46:54,172 --> 01:46:55,782
Inshallah.

976
01:46:56,216 --> 01:46:59,196
Here are the
Hatuns who were raised by mother Selcan...

977
01:47:00,310 --> 01:47:03,450
Your soul shall rest in peace, mother.

978
01:47:08,564 --> 01:47:10,794
Your children work for your tribe.

979
01:47:14,416 --> 01:47:16,426
Hand it to me, my Alaeddin.

980
01:47:19,994 --> 01:47:22,554
Masha Allah (praise be) to my kids!

981
01:47:25,785 --> 01:47:27,355
My valiants!

982
01:47:30,772 --> 01:47:34,302
Now that we are not allowed to join war,
we want to help.

983
01:47:35,308 --> 01:47:38,138
Masha Allah!
Your time will come.

984
01:47:38,193 --> 01:47:42,333
You'll sweat over your trainings
until your time comes.

985
01:47:44,809 --> 01:47:47,339
Mother Bala is right, my lion.

986
01:47:47,975 --> 01:47:49,915
Your time is soon.

987
01:47:52,801 --> 01:47:55,491
Don't tire yourself more,
beautiful daughter.

988
01:47:58,202 --> 01:48:02,372
Where are you taking the
ammunations, mother? Can we help on the way?

989
01:48:04,882 --> 01:48:09,732
We will take the ammunation to
Inegol Castle with sisters, Alaeddin.

990
01:48:21,486 --> 01:48:24,506
Who is it coming, Baysungur?
Why are the drums being beaten?

991
01:48:24,876 --> 01:48:27,726
Holofire's aunt's soldiers have arrived,
Malhun Hatun.

992
01:48:31,179 --> 01:48:34,239
They have come a long way.
We should host them.

993
01:48:34,313 --> 01:48:38,213
Take them to the guest tents.
I'll them her when I am available.

994
01:48:50,377 --> 01:48:52,727
Come on!
Everybody back to their job!

995
01:48:52,753 --> 01:48:54,913
Go rest, kids.

996
01:49:03,983 --> 01:49:06,663
Osman has nothing in his hand.

997
01:49:06,679 --> 01:49:08,646
I ruined his quarters.

998
01:49:08,646 --> 01:49:12,246
I took his ammunation that he has
saved for years.

999
01:49:12,663 --> 01:49:15,443
And most importantly, mines!

1000
01:49:15,477 --> 01:49:18,540
Thanks to Master Arius cleverness!

1001
01:49:18,540 --> 01:49:20,960
Osman is nothing without mines!

1002
01:49:22,628 --> 01:49:25,208
He is still a great danger.

1003
01:49:25,979 --> 01:49:28,609
But I need to give it to Arius.

1004
01:49:29,012 --> 01:49:31,532
He always has a plan for future.

1005
01:49:32,071 --> 01:49:35,321
This is why we call him master Arius,
Romanus.

1006
01:49:36,098 --> 01:49:40,438
I think you need to call him
master Arius as well.

1007
01:49:41,729 --> 01:49:46,999
As you can understand from the silence,
he must have already claimed the mines.

1008
01:49:47,700 --> 01:49:50,110
How would that be possible?

1009
01:49:50,110 --> 01:49:55,050
They were to sneak into near our castle,
build a quarters, and attack with catapults!

1010
01:49:55,201 --> 01:49:56,691
Is that so? Hah!

1011
01:49:56,979 --> 01:50:00,939
We only stopped their next attack, Nikola!

1012
01:50:03,850 --> 01:50:06,540
And I am bored of talking about it.

1013
01:50:09,865 --> 01:50:14,425
When Arius comes,
I'll form a great army.

1014
01:50:17,779 --> 01:50:20,519
I am not here to stand behind the walls.

1015
01:50:22,802 --> 01:50:24,602
I am here to shed blood!

1016
01:51:29,122 --> 01:51:30,552
Thank you.

1017
01:51:31,485 --> 01:51:33,095
Thank you.

1018
01:51:35,304 --> 01:51:36,974
Ey Masha Allah!

1019
01:51:39,154 --> 01:51:43,564
Brother!
Tell me, what is the situation?

1020
01:51:44,054 --> 01:51:46,004
Those are the last ones.

1021
01:51:46,004 --> 01:51:47,795
When we move these too...

1022
01:51:47,795 --> 01:51:52,415
all the catapults will be deployed
in front of Inegol Castle, my Bey.

1023
01:51:52,557 --> 01:51:54,467
What about their strength?

1024
01:51:55,105 --> 01:51:57,205
Are our catapults powerful, brother?

1025
01:51:57,900 --> 01:52:01,710
Everything is all ready, right?

1026
01:52:02,724 --> 01:52:05,164
They are powerful, Osman Bey.
Don't worry.

1027
01:52:05,878 --> 01:52:09,248
We will demolish Inegol walls with
these catapults with Allah's permission.

1028
01:52:10,736 --> 01:52:12,136
Inshallah.

1029
01:52:13,448 --> 01:52:15,528
We will do it with these Inshallah.

1030
01:52:38,637 --> 01:52:41,577
We turned the villagers on their way,
my Bey.

1031
01:52:41,766 --> 01:52:44,156
They won't help Inegol.

1032
01:52:45,014 --> 01:52:48,934
Another caravan was coming,
we took care of them.

1033
01:52:49,760 --> 01:52:53,290
You took care of one, what about the rest?

1034
01:52:53,751 --> 01:52:59,321
The roads are in Kayi's control.
Nothing enters, nothing goes out.

1035
01:53:06,574 --> 01:53:09,664
We blocked all the aid ways to Inegol.

1036
01:53:11,770 --> 01:53:15,340
There is no obstacle left for it to
be Turk's property.

1037
01:53:17,799 --> 01:53:20,259
They think we have stopped.

1038
01:53:24,004 --> 01:53:28,544
However, we will keep coming at
the cruels.

1039
01:53:50,950 --> 01:53:53,110
- Sir.
- Talk.

1040
01:53:53,157 --> 01:53:56,177
Sir, it's Osman.
Osman and Turks are coming.

1041
01:53:56,626 --> 01:54:00,186
Catapults, battering rams and
many equipments.

1042
01:54:02,800 --> 01:54:05,260
If you've burned the catapults...

1043
01:54:06,512 --> 01:54:08,582
what are the ones that are coming?

1044
01:54:14,501 --> 01:54:17,971
Do you know about the Zumruduanka Bird?

1045
01:54:19,042 --> 01:54:21,112
It's name is Turk!

1046
01:54:22,962 --> 01:54:29,132
We will resurrect from where we burn

1047
01:54:29,132 --> 01:54:31,249
Peace be to Allah.

1048
01:54:31,435 --> 01:54:34,195
Burn it Nikola, burn it!

1049
01:54:34,777 --> 01:54:37,867
Your prepare your fire in hell!

1050
01:54:39,585 --> 01:54:42,165
Zumruduanka.

1051
01:54:46,288 --> 01:54:48,498
Zumruduanka.

1052
01:54:48,951 --> 01:54:50,551
How did they do it?

1053
01:54:51,266 --> 01:54:52,926
How?

1054
01:54:53,206 --> 01:54:54,287
Damn it!

1055
01:54:54,287 --> 01:54:56,251
How many catapults are there?

1056
01:54:56,251 --> 01:54:59,151
Sir, I counted five but
I couldn't count th...

1057
01:55:00,613 --> 01:55:03,715
Ah!
I only broke the branches of the tree!

1058
01:55:03,715 --> 01:55:06,295
The roots of that tree
reaches up to my castle!

1059
01:55:11,029 --> 01:55:13,379
What are you saying Nikola?

1060
01:55:14,669 --> 01:55:16,309
Speak clearly.

1061
01:55:18,596 --> 01:55:21,496
The trade they did to Inegol, Romanus.

1062
01:55:21,793 --> 01:55:24,243
The caravans that carried their goods...

1063
01:55:24,903 --> 01:55:28,173
...the caravans that carry their goods...

1064
01:55:28,713 --> 01:55:33,953
They only carried their ammunation.

1065
01:55:35,290 --> 01:55:37,060
For years.

1066
01:55:38,020 --> 01:55:42,740
While we were asking to ourselves
"Where is that quarters of Osman?! Where?!"

1067
01:55:43,919 --> 01:55:46,719
They builded the quarters
in front of us!

1068
01:55:47,218 --> 01:55:49,148
We couldn't see!

1069
01:55:51,275 --> 01:55:54,125
You were the one who should have seen.

1070
01:55:59,670 --> 01:56:01,810
You should have seen it.

1071
01:56:04,758 --> 01:56:07,598
Our plan is obvious!

1072
01:56:09,075 --> 01:56:12,355
We will do what we do the best.

1073
01:56:14,644 --> 01:56:16,764
We will fight!

1074
01:56:27,058 --> 01:56:29,438
We will fight.

1075
01:56:47,823 --> 01:56:49,873
Alps!

1076
01:56:50,976 --> 01:56:52,856
Brothers!

1077
01:56:53,896 --> 01:56:56,436
Inegol's walls are strong.

1078
01:56:56,904 --> 01:57:01,684
But not as strong as our ambition.

1079
01:57:04,954 --> 01:57:10,444
Now that they don't accept
surrendering with peace...

1080
01:57:13,016 --> 01:57:15,556
...now it's our time.

1081
01:57:17,165 --> 01:57:20,315
We'll put a hole in Inegol walls.

1082
01:57:20,984 --> 01:57:22,734
When the soldiers start moving...

1083
01:57:23,638 --> 01:57:28,198
...our archers will start shooting
their archers on the walls.

1084
01:57:30,700 --> 01:57:34,230
But when you try to enter the castle
from those holes...

1085
01:57:35,619 --> 01:57:40,419
...they'll pour boiling oil
from the castle.

1086
01:57:42,511 --> 01:57:44,861
We will be cautious!

1087
01:57:45,549 --> 01:57:49,359
Brothers, may our fight be blessed!

1088
01:57:55,346 --> 01:58:26,706
Allah is the greatest!

1089
01:58:30,676 --> 01:58:32,196
My Bey!

1090
01:58:32,438 --> 01:58:33,928
They are approaching!

1091
01:58:52,197 --> 01:58:54,037
They are approaching, yeah.

1092
01:58:55,181 --> 01:58:58,491
Which Turkmen Bey could
stop himself from joining war?

1093
01:59:00,751 --> 01:59:02,641
They are approaching!

1094
01:59:05,994 --> 01:59:08,394
They are approaching.

1095
01:59:09,366 --> 01:59:11,376
Byzantine's brave men!

1096
01:59:12,700 --> 01:59:14,260
My soldiers!

1097
01:59:14,708 --> 01:59:17,538
The day has come.

1098
01:59:18,601 --> 01:59:21,251
The enemy who
made a nest in front of our home

1099
01:59:21,521 --> 01:59:23,581
is now at the door of our castle!

1100
01:59:27,463 --> 01:59:30,663
I, Aya Nikola...

1101
01:59:31,903 --> 01:59:36,223
...have felt death at my neck for years.

1102
01:59:37,391 --> 01:59:41,471
But I wasn't afraid. I am not afraid.
I will not be afraid!

1103
01:59:44,394 --> 01:59:46,594
What are we going to do?

1104
01:59:47,124 --> 01:59:49,554
We will cut their breath!

1105
01:59:50,068 --> 01:59:54,128
My soldiers! Today you need to entitle...

1106
01:59:54,650 --> 01:59:58,190
...your swords and shields!

1107
01:59:58,996 --> 02:00:03,906
Death is at the edge of our swords today.

1108
02:00:05,666 --> 02:00:09,716
And we will kill Turks...

1109
02:00:10,618 --> 02:00:14,848
with these swords in İnegöl.

1110
02:00:18,507 --> 02:00:21,667
They will make breaches in our walls.

1111
02:00:23,424 --> 02:00:29,164
Don't be afraid and don't step back.

1112
02:00:29,385 --> 02:00:33,175
Don't! Because...

1113
02:00:33,455 --> 02:00:38,765
we will put Turks' skulls in
those breaches.

1114
02:00:43,294 --> 02:00:47,294
My soldiers! Byzantine's brave men...

1115
02:00:47,957 --> 02:00:52,747
I, Aya Nikola...

1116
02:00:53,404 --> 02:00:55,654
am not afraid!

1117
02:00:56,408 --> 02:00:58,458
Don't you be afraid too.

1118
02:00:59,028 --> 02:01:04,578
Who wants the shed the blood of
Turks with me?

1119
02:01:04,612 --> 02:01:05,912
Us!

1120
02:01:05,969 --> 02:01:09,969
- Who?
- Us!

1121
02:01:26,709 --> 02:01:29,729
Sir, a riderless horse came here.

1122
02:02:09,761 --> 02:02:11,551
Master Arius

1123
02:02:24,669 --> 02:02:26,369
Osman.

1124
02:02:29,150 --> 02:02:31,230
I promise you.

1125
02:02:32,792 --> 02:02:38,662
I will exhibit Osman's
head in every tribe.

1126
02:02:42,065 --> 02:02:45,205
I promise.

1127
02:03:02,305 --> 02:03:05,485
I'm waiting outside the castle walls.

1128
02:03:05,877 --> 02:03:07,837
Osman Bey.

1129
02:03:17,753 --> 02:03:21,753
Prepare faster.
Come on.

1130
02:03:33,773 --> 02:03:37,773
Wait for me, Osman.

1131
02:03:42,713 --> 02:03:44,093
Wait.

1132
02:03:53,701 --> 02:03:57,321
Osman Bey, we're here to support you.

1133
02:04:00,526 --> 02:04:03,426
Thank you.

1134
02:04:05,464 --> 02:04:08,404
Welcome, Turkmen Beys.

1135
02:04:08,813 --> 02:04:11,103
Thank you.

1136
02:04:12,214 --> 02:04:15,464
For how long do you not
inform us about the raids?

1137
02:04:15,946 --> 02:04:18,886
We didn't hear your call, Osman Bey.

1138
02:04:20,497 --> 02:04:24,007
Every horse takes you to İnegöl.

1139
02:04:25,464 --> 02:04:29,464
The war is here. The conquest is here.

1140
02:04:30,447 --> 02:04:34,447
You don't need to be informed. You
know now.

1141
02:04:38,159 --> 02:04:41,679
Thank you. Okay, then.

1142
02:04:45,004 --> 02:04:47,874
Turkmen Beys...

1143
02:04:48,323 --> 02:04:51,523
you accepted to come here
for the conquest.

1144
02:04:52,412 --> 02:04:56,412
Thank you all.
Welcome.

1145
02:04:56,506 --> 02:04:59,666
Thank you, my Bey.

1146
02:05:02,203 --> 02:05:04,863
You're under my command now.

1147
02:05:05,118 --> 02:05:10,508
Your Alps will go inside the
breaches with Boran and Konur.

1148
02:05:10,892 --> 02:05:16,152
The rest of them will attack from
behind with Turgut Bey.

1149
02:05:19,197 --> 02:05:21,737
Those who will come with me...

1150
02:05:21,939 --> 02:05:24,679
will break the door of the castle and...

1151
02:05:24,729 --> 02:05:27,359
will go inside.

1152
02:05:29,503 --> 02:05:32,263
There will be not only us.

1153
02:05:32,515 --> 02:05:38,525
Many valiants will also be there.

1154
02:05:41,782 --> 02:05:47,182
We haven't stopped since my grandfather Süleyman
Shah and my father Ertuğrul Ghazi.

1155
02:05:47,675 --> 02:05:51,335
We won't stop too, and the ones who
will come after us.

1156
02:05:54,039 --> 02:05:57,459
May our war be blessed.

1157
02:05:59,965 --> 02:06:24,825
- Allah-u Akbar!
- Allah-u Akbar!

1158
02:06:35,203 --> 02:06:38,563
My Bey, the doors are opened.

1159
02:06:38,639 --> 02:06:41,139
The news are spread.

1160
02:06:54,528 --> 02:06:56,208
Come.

1161
02:06:56,468 --> 02:06:58,738
Come here.

1162
02:06:58,830 --> 02:07:04,180
I will send your food now, you
can rest then.

1163
02:07:04,496 --> 02:07:09,636
We're thankful but why is the
tent in a hurry?

1164
02:07:09,703 --> 02:07:12,023
Has something dangerous happened?

1165
02:07:12,610 --> 02:07:16,610
Nothing to worry about. As
I said, you can rest...

1166
02:07:16,788 --> 02:07:20,048
then, Malhun Hatun will talk to you.

1167
02:07:30,653 --> 02:07:35,293
You can rest now, we will take action
at the night.

1168
02:08:42,165 --> 02:08:45,775
- Nikola.
- Osman Bey.

1169
02:08:47,944 --> 02:08:50,844
Give us the castle, peacefully.

1170
02:08:51,877 --> 02:08:56,987
Both your castle and your soldiers will
not be harmed.

1171
02:08:58,312 --> 02:09:02,312
Don't worry, I will forgive them all.

1172
02:09:02,702 --> 02:09:06,122
Will you? Huh?

1173
02:09:06,845 --> 02:09:10,015
You're underrating me, Osman Bey.

1174
02:09:10,265 --> 02:09:14,425
We have been fighting for years.

1175
02:09:16,160 --> 02:09:18,650
Do you think I will give you my castle?

1176
02:09:18,750 --> 02:09:23,440
I enslaved many of your acquaintances,
from your family, from your tent...

1177
02:09:23,563 --> 02:09:28,813
I also tortured your Alps there.

1178
02:09:31,319 --> 02:09:35,319
I won't give you my castle.
I have a memory of it.

1179
02:09:36,648 --> 02:09:39,408
That's why I pity you.

1180
02:09:42,263 --> 02:09:44,423
You will lose everything that belongs
to you.

1181
02:09:46,140 --> 02:09:47,680
Your castle...

1182
02:09:48,835 --> 02:09:50,655
Your life...

1183
02:09:57,401 --> 02:10:02,111
If you don't surrender, too much
blood will be shed.

1184
02:10:03,557 --> 02:10:05,567
You know me well.

1185
02:10:09,172 --> 02:10:11,632
I will shed blood.

1186
02:10:12,141 --> 02:10:14,991
Your blood will be shed more than ours.

1187
02:10:17,902 --> 02:10:21,032
Osman Bey, this is İnegöl.

1188
02:10:22,328 --> 02:10:24,898
My land.

1189
02:10:27,159 --> 02:10:28,759
I'm not afraid.

1190
02:10:31,309 --> 02:10:33,889
My soldiers are not afraid.

1191
02:10:39,721 --> 02:10:42,181
I'm warning you one last time.

1192
02:10:44,565 --> 02:10:46,755
Give us the castle.

1193
02:10:48,453 --> 02:10:54,133
This land's winds are
for Islam flag to fly.

1194
02:10:54,684 --> 02:10:59,154
The wind isn't for İnegöl's walls.

1195
02:10:59,801 --> 02:11:03,301
There are enough dungeons
for you in my castle and...

1196
02:11:03,941 --> 02:11:07,581
there are enough swords to kill you.

1197
02:11:23,969 --> 02:11:25,819
Is this your decision?

1198
02:11:27,621 --> 02:11:30,741
Yes, it is.

1199
02:11:32,192 --> 02:11:37,722
İnegöl is here, come and take it.
If you can.

1200
02:11:43,466 --> 02:11:46,496
I did what I had to do.

1201
02:11:47,983 --> 02:11:49,783
Okay, then.

1202
02:11:54,399 --> 02:11:59,329
We will use our power on İnegöl.

1203
02:12:05,923 --> 02:12:08,933
İnegöl belongs to Islam now.

1204
02:12:47,938 --> 02:12:52,948
We are the children of those who
aren't afraid to ride anywhere.

1205
02:12:54,652 --> 02:12:58,192
We have waited for İnegöl for so much.

1206
02:12:59,570 --> 02:13:02,090
Tell the Beys.

1207
02:13:02,413 --> 02:13:04,683
Tell the Alps.

1208
02:13:05,447 --> 02:13:09,917
Take the catapult, prepare
the battering ram.

1209
02:13:11,128 --> 02:13:15,128
Sharpen your swords one last time.

1210
02:13:21,568 --> 02:13:24,448
It's time for conquest.

1211
02:13:26,174 --> 02:13:59,404
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com